## P5 reproduced P4 exactly

Across all natural and Gate-P symbolic cases, P5 matched P4-propagated exactly on final digest, multiplications, pair terms, peak monomials, evaluated ANF nodes, candidate decisions, reject reasons, accepted/shared counts, estimated costs, and folds consumed.

Gate-P totals for both P4 and P5:

- demanded binary nodes checked: **322**;
- demanded propagated candidates: **181**;
- accepted/consumed folds: **29 / 29**;
- accepted shared folds: **22**;
- propagated signature/candidate nodes present in the constructed DAG: **520**.

Thus P5 changed representation and cost placement, not the optimization policy or mathematical work.

## Gate-P work reduction versus direct

The P5/P4 fold behavior is identical, so the symbolic reductions remain the P4 reductions:

- multiplications: **0.3360x** direct;
- pair terms: **0.0984x** direct;
- evaluated ANF nodes: **0.5415x** direct;
- peak monomials: **0.8973x** direct.

P5 lowering is therefore still substantially faster than direct, but it is **16.4% slower than P4 lowering** because P5 deliberately moves candidate-cost arithmetic from construction to demand time.

## Construction cost improvement

P4's simultaneous Gate-P metadata build was **5.6693x** ordinary construction. P5 reduced that to **2.5611x**, or **54.8% less build time than P4**.

The full P5 pipeline is **0.5790x P4**, a **42.1% reduction**. It crosses below direct in **8/36** Gate-P cases, versus only 3/36 for P4 in the previous architecture.

