## Memory diagnostics

Predeclared full-pipeline traced Python peak on Gate-P:

- P5 / direct: **0.7910x**;
- P5 / P4: **0.6989x**.

A separate post-hoc build-only `tracemalloc` diagnostic found P5 construction peak **1.1753x direct** but only **0.5841x P4**. In other words, the packed metadata itself still costs memory relative to an unannotated builder, but much less than P4's object-rich metadata; downstream ANF savings then make the complete P5 pipeline peak lower than direct on Gate-P.

